<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adalbert II of Tuscany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 915</span> · Also known as Adalbert the Rich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adalbert II, called the Rich, was margrave of Tuscany from 886 until his death in 915, ruling from Lucca. The son of Adalbert I, he made the margraves among the most powerful lords in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and played a leading part in the struggles for the Italian crown. His marriage to Bertha, daughter of the Carolingian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-ii">Lothair II</a>, raised the standing of his house.</p></div>
